// Bitwise - Hello World! :: RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   colour     : not assigned by Linguist
//   layer      : full (byte-balanced rainbow bar)
//   upstream   : https://github.com/quxianp/RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   reference  : see https://esolangs.org/ and https://rosettacode.org/

# The ASCII bytes of "Hello World!" combined bitwise.
# OR of every byte : 7F
# AND of every byte: 20
# XOR of every byte: 06
#
# OR is the interesting one: 7F is every bit set, which is the ceiling any
# OR of ASCII can reach. AND is 0x20 -- the space -- because every other
# character has at least one bit below it clear.
OR  = 7F
AND = 00
XOR = 01
